In case anyone comes searching for this issue or error message later on, here's a more complete example:

```
// index.js
export * from "./B";
export * from "./A";
```

```
// A.js
import {B} from ".";
export class A extends B {}
```

```
// B.js
export class B {}
```

When we try to import the commonjs compiled output from these three files, `A` will attempt to create a function passing in `B`, but `B` will not be defined yet and you'll get the error:

`Super expression must either be null or a function`
